<article class="env-lemma" id="03FY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03FY">Lemma <span data-tag="03FY">66.6.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. There exists a Zariski covering $X = \bigcup X_ i$ such that each algebraic space $X_ i$ has a surjective étale covering by an affine scheme. We may in addition assume each $X_ i$ maps into an affine open of $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/03FX" data-tag="03FX">66.6.1</a> we can find a surjective étale morphism $U = \coprod U_ i \to X$, with $U_ i$ affine and mapping into an affine open of $S$. Let $X_ i \subset X$ be the open subspace of $X$ such that $U_ i \to X$ factors through an étale surjective morphism $U_ i \to X_ i$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/06NF" data-tag="06NF">66.4.10</a>. Since $U = \bigcup U_ i$ we see that $X = \bigcup X_ i$. As $U_ i \to X_ i$ is surjective it follows that $X_ i \to S$ maps into an affine open of $S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>